===Etymology 2===
The {{glossary|adjective}} is derived from {{der|en|frm|sublime|t=admirable, excellent, perfect; placed in a high position; reaching a great height; of a person: of high office or rank}} (modern {{cog|fr|sublime}}), and from its {{glossary|etymon}} {{der|en|la|sublīmis}}, {{m|la|sublīmus|t=elevated, raised; exalted, uplifted, sublime|pos=adjective}}: see [[#Etymology 1|etymology 1]].<ref name="OED adj">{{R:OED Online|pos=adj.'' and ''n|id=8404089130|date=September 2023|nodot=1}}; {{R:Lexico|pos=adj}}</ref>
 
The {{glossary|noun}} is derived from {{der|en|frm|sublime|t=elevated style in writing; quality in art or nature inspiring awe, reverence, etc.}} (modern {{cog|fr|sublime}}), from the adjective: see further above.<ref name="OED adj"/>

